  <page>
    <title>Silja Line</title>
    <id>83397</id>
    <revision>
      <id>37072663</id>
      <timestamp>2006-01-28T12:27:20Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>84.137.29.245</ip>
      </contributor>
      <comment>/* External links */ This weblink is fine for &quot;GTS Finnjet&quot; but has no relevance concerning this article</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">[[Image:Silja Line ships in Helsinki 2004.jpg|thumb|300px|Silja Line ships in [[Helsinki]].]]
'''Silja Line''' ('''Silja Oyj Apb''') is a [[Finland|Finnish]] shipping company owned by the multinational [[Sea Containers]]. Silja operates multiple [[ferry]] lines on the [[Baltic Sea]]. It is among the biggest operators on its core market, transporting about five million passengers and over 300,000 cars every year.

==Fleet==
*[[M/S Silja Serenade|M/S ''Silja Serenade'']], [[Helsinki]]&amp;mdash;[[Mariehamn]]&amp;mdash;[[Stockholm]]
*[[M/S Silja Symphony|M/S ''Silja Symphony'']], Helsinki&amp;mdash;Mariehamn&amp;mdash;Stockholm
*[[M/S Silja Europa|M/S ''Silja Europa'']], [[Turku]]&amp;mdash;Mariehamn/[[Långnäs]]&amp;mdash;Stockholm/[[Kapellskär]] (Kapellskär only in winters)
*[[M/S Silja Festival|M/S ''Silja Festival'']], Turku&amp;mdash;Mariehamn/Långnäs&amp;mdash;Stockholm
*[[M/S SuperSeaCat One|M/S ''SuperSeaCat One'']], Helsinki&amp;mdash;Tallinn
*[[M/S SuperSeaCat Three|M/S ''SuperSeaCat Three'']], Helsinki&amp;mdash;Tallinn
*[[M/S SuperSeaCat Four|M/S ''SuperSeaCat Four'']], Helsinki&amp;mdash;Tallinn
*[[M/S Silja Opera|M/S ''Silja Opera'']], Cruises on the Baltic Sea

== See also ==
*[[Euroway]]
*[[SeaWind Line]]
*[[Viking Line]] rival operator

==External links==
*[http://www.silja.com/ Official site - silja.com]
*[http://www.siljaweb.com/ SILJAweb.com]

[[Category:Shipping companies]]
[[Category:Ferry systems]]
[[Category:Companies of Finland]]
[[Category:Shipping in Scandinavia]]

[[de:Silja Line]]
[[fi:Silja Line]]
[[sv:Silja Line]]</text>
