      <text xml:space="preserve">'''UIN''' was coined by [[Mirabilis (company)|Mirabilis]], to be used as the name of the '''Unique Identification Number''' that each user of the [[ICQ]] [[instant messaging]] software is assigned upon registration. Unlike most other instant messaging programs, in ICQ the only information that is permanent to a registered user is the UIN. The screen name may be changed at will, without having to reregister.

See [[ICQ]] for further information.

