      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Eurysthenes''' ({{lang-el|Εὐρυσθένης}}) was one of the [[Heracleidae]], a great-great-great-grandson of [[Heracles]], and a son of [[Aristodemus]].  His twin was [[Procles]], and together they received the land of [[Lacedaemon]] after [[Cresphontes]], [[Temenus]] and [[Oxylus]] captured the [[Peloponnesus]].

{{Greek-myth-stub}}

