  <page>
    <title>Iasus</title>
    <id>83615</id>
    <revision>
      <id>15974997</id>
      <timestamp>2005-05-20T22:43:15Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>D6</username>
        <id>75561</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>{{[[Template:disambig|disambig]]}}</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Iasus''' was the name of several individuals:

*'''Iasus''' was the father of [[Atalanta]] by [[Clymene]]; he was the son of King [[Lycurgus]] of [[Arcadia]].
*'''Iasus''' was one of the [[Dactyl (mythology)|Dactyli]], the son of [[Rhea (mythology)|Rhea]] and [[Anchiale]].
*'''Iasus''' was the king of [[Argos]].  He was the son of either [[Argus]] ([[Panoptes]]) and [[Ecbasus]], or [[Triopas]] and [[Ismene]].
*'''Iasus''' was killed by [[Aeneas]] in the [[Trojan War]].

{{disambig}}

[[de:Iasos]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
