      <contributor>
        <username>Tordek ar</username>
        <id>80653</id>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Phyleus''' was a son of King [[Augeas]] of [[Elis]] and father of [[Meges]].  He supported [[Heracles]] instead of his father (in the matter of the Augean Stables) and was exiled.  After Heracles killed Augeas, he gave Phyleus the kingdom.
{{myth-stub}}
[[Category:Greek mythological people]]

[[es:Fileo]]
[[fr:Phylée]]</text>
