  <page>
    <title>Automedon</title>
    <id>83630</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41592803</id>
      <timestamp>2006-02-28T10:23:41Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>FlaBot</username>
        <id>228773</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <comment>robot  Adding: pl</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Automedon''', son of [[Diores]], was [[Achilles]]' charioteer.  In [[Homer]]'s ''[[Iliad]]'', he rides into battle once [[Patroclus]] has donned Achilles' armor, commanding Achilles' horses [[Balius and Xanthos]].  After Patroclos's death, Automedon is driven to the rear of the battle, where he attempts to console the bereaved horses.  Zeus finally intervenes, and Automedon resumes driving the chariot, but can not aid the [[Achaeans]] until [[Alcimidon]] agrees to be his driver.  He repels an attempt on his life by [[Hector]], [[Aeneas]], [[Chromios]], and [[Aretos]], killing Aretos and taking his armor in the process.

''[[Iliad]]'' XVI, 145; XVII, 429

''[[Iliad]]'' XIX, XXIII, XIV '''are not covered'''.

{{Greek-myth-stub}}

[[Category:People who fought in the Trojan War]]

[[pl:Automedon]]</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Diores</title>
    <id>83631</id>
    <revision>
      <id>22467069</id>
      <timestamp>2005-09-03T12:23:41Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <ip>84.64.37.31</ip>
      </contributor>
      <text xml:space="preserve">In [[Greek mythology]], '''Diorês''' referred to two different people.

*One was the father of [[Automedon]].
*One was the son of [[Amarynceus]] ('''Diorês Amaryngkëidês''')

{{disambig}}</text>
    </revision>
  </page>
  <page>
    <title>Azan</title>
    <id>83632</id>
    <revision>
      <id>31406264</id>
      <timestamp>2005-12-15T01:12:55Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>CyberSkull</username>
        <id>123609</id>
      </contributor>
      <comment>dablinks</comment>
      <text xml:space="preserve">{{dablink|For the Islamic call to prayer, see [[Adhan|Azaan]].}}
{{dablink|For the ''[[Star Trek]]'' character, see [[Azan (Star Trek)]].}}

In [[Greek mythology]], '''Azan''' was the son of [[Arcas]] and [[Erato]].  [[Azania]] in [[Arcadia]] was named for him.

[[Category:Greek mythological people]]
{{Greek-myth-stub}}</text>
    </revision>
