  <page>
    <title>Caguas, Puerto Rico</title>
    <id>83709</id>
    <revision>
      <id>41724909</id>
      <timestamp>2006-03-01T08:32:52Z</timestamp>
      <contributor>
        <username>AntonioMartin</username>
        <id>4042</id>
      </contributor>
      <minor />
      <text xml:space="preserve">'''Caguas''' (founded in 1775) is a [[Municipalities of Puerto Rico|municipality]] located in the eastern central area of [[Puerto Rico]]. It is known as ''El Valle Del Turabo'' (''Turabo Valley'') or ''La Ciudad Criolla'' (''The Creole City'') and its name originates from the [[Taíno]] [[cacique]] [[Caguax]].

Caguas is located one half hour by car from [[San Juan, Puerto Rico|San Juan]] and one and a half hours from [[Ponce, Puerto Rico|Ponce]].

Natives of Caguas are called '''cagüeños'''.

Caguas is the sister city of [[Hartford,_Connecticut|Hartford,Connecticut]].

[[Image:Caguas cathedral.jpg|thumb|right|293px|Caguas cathedral Dulce Nombre de Jesús inaugurated in 1930 with image of [[Carlos Manuel Rodríguez]] (beatified 1999)]]
